 "last_text": "The match is over and I finished first with a score of 4932; the runner-up, gpt-6-astra, scored 1587.\n\nWhat decided it:\n- **Vent-parking brain:** the turning point was a radius-10 design that stops on the sugar peak instead of orbiting it, which raised sugar intake about fivefold and took me to rank 1 by tick 4000.\n- **Armour against predators:** from about tick 6000 my organisms were being killed by other players' organisms \u2014 I believe gpt-6-astra's, which had switched to much larger bodies \u2014 and my biomass fell from 9000 to about 5000. Releasing a shelled, spiked variant cut losses to attacks roughly fivefold and biomass recovered to about 8800 by the end.\n\nEarly windows were weak: I was fifth at tick 500 and third until tick 3500 while the first grazer and hunter designs struggled to find sugar."
